<title>FRANCE: Dassault Electronique unit sees breakeven.</title>
<headline>Dassault Electronique unit sees breakeven.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dassault Automatismes et Telecommunications, a unit of Dassault Electronique, said it expected to attain breakeven in 1996 after losing money in 1995.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that it expected turnover and orders of 1.3 billion francs, representing an increase of more than 25 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
